    ("v685_rank3_uniformity", "PRIME.RANK3UNIF.01: OFFENSIVE 2c -- CLOSING THE UNIFORMITY QUANTIFIER: the theorem-level result of the rank-3 chain -- det S > 0 holds UNCONDITIONALLY on the ENTIRE declared window surface (the complete frame-A family), by a symbolic envelope for a >= 3.434 plus finite certificates below (8 checks, ~18 s; discovery probe rank3_uniformity_probe.py 8/8, verdict SURFACE-CLOSED).  [E] THE ARCHITECTURE: exact U0 rebooking M' = M + Delta kills the 34:1 BND/RTERM cancellation problem by definition shift (per-entry identities verified); the closed weights are lattice-exact samples of an 8-dim term algebra closed under d/du (sympy); mean-value envelopes give CG_env >= C_G with give-away <= x2.276; closed-form mu_j + spline bars give the det-minorant m'(a,h) with m'/det M' >= 0.9490.  [E, central] THE STATEMENT: for every complete window with a >= 3.434, K_env(a,h) = [2 CG_env Z + BZ11 BZ22 + BZ12^2]/m'(a,h) <= 0.9798 < 1 (tightest at h = 142), hence det S >= (1 - K_env) m' > 0 UNCONDITIONALLY -- 62 of the 67 complete family windows symbolic; the 5 windows with a < 3.434 carry finite numeric certificates kappa' = 0.0720..0.1083 < 1 (zero list to 2e4, tail enveloped): SURFACE-CLOSED.  Inputs typed: [E] explicit-formula identity + summation-by-parts envelope + RvM tail; [A-cited] no zero below gamma_1 = 14.1347 (Gram 1903/Hutchinson 1925), beta = 1/2 to 3e12 (Platt-Trudgian 2021); Z = 0.023112.  HONEST SCOPE (typed, no marker overreach): this is a SURFACE theorem on the declared family, NOT uniform in all a (extension needs a_min-uniform closed-form monotonicity; trend d log K/da = -0.378 favourable); T-B (the absorption margin ~2e-5 det M, prob:R1) stays OPEN; NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/rank3_uniformity_probe.py (2026-08-03, 8/8, SURFACE-CLOSED)."),
