    ("v689_gaussian_code_bridge", "E8.GAUSSCODE.01: the Gaussian code bridge (review contract E8.GAUSSIAN.CODE.01) -- E8(Z[i])/(1+i) IS the information space of RM(1,3): the mu4 complex structure J makes E8 a rank-4 Z[i]-lattice L; reduction modulo the ramified Gaussian prime (1+i) gives L/(1+i)L = F2^4 EXACTLY (26 checks, ~3 s, exact integer/Fraction arithmetic, sympy only for the Smith normal form; discovery probe gaussian_code_bridge_probe.py 26/26, verdict GAUSSIAN-CODE-BRIDGE-EXACT).  [E] SNF exact; standard E8 model cross-check: basis |det| = 256 = 2^8 (doubled coordinates), SNF [1,1,1,1,2,2,2,2] -- presentation-independent.  [E] THE CENSUS: 240 roots fall 15 x 16 over the nontrivial classes (the zero class PROVABLY EMPTY), each class a union of 4 of the 60 G31 lines (60 = 15 x 4).  [E] THE SEMANTICS: sigma = c^4 acts on the quotient as the RM(1,3) family permutation (3-cycle on the family bits F1 -> F2 -> F3 -> F1 + fixed anchor, exactly the v638 info-bit action); the residual gauge = centralizer of the family 3-cycle in GL(4, F2) has order 18 (= 6 x 3 equivariant isomorphisms); the coordinate block = the sum-of-families label F1 + F2 + F3.  MUST-FAIL CONTROLS all fire: the naive placement keeps the 15 x 16 census (a property of (E8, J) alone) but the sigma-bit-semantics becomes UNDEFINED (witness codeword lift off the lattice); a non-piJ placement has NO Z[i]-module at all; Z[i]^4 trivializes (only 16 minimal vectors, 11 classes empty -- no 240, no 15 x 16, no RM(1,3)).  No marker move.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/gaussian_code_bridge_probe.py (2026-08-03, 26/26, GAUSSIAN-CODE-BRIDGE-EXACT)."),
    ("v690_quartic_half", "E8.QUARTICHALF.01: the quartic invariant restriction (review contract E8.QUARTIC.HALF.01) -- is G31 the holomorphic mu4 shadow of the E8 Coxeter compiler?  ALIVE, with the honest split (22 checks, ~1 s, exact Gaussian-integer/Fraction arithmetic, no floats; discovery probe quartic_half_probe.py 22/22, verdict QUARTIC-HALF-ALIVE).  [PROOF, typed honest] THE VANISHING HALF {2,14,18,30} is TRUE but TRIVIAL: W(J alpha) = -i W(alpha) for all 240 roots => every J-orbit contributes t^d (1 + (-i)^d + (-1)^d + i^d) -- identically zero for every d != 0 mod 4, so the mechanism holds for 6, 10, 22, 26 too (mu4 orbit factor, NOT degree-list-specific); degrees 4/6 vanish on ANY q-isotropic subspace (f_4 = 576 q^2, f_6 = 1920 q^3 as symbolic 8-variable identities); F_4| has all 35 monomial coefficients = 0 exactly (the first G31-consistency point).  [E, central] THE LOAD-BEARING CONTENT: F_8|, F_12|, F_20|, F_24| are G31-invariant (all 60 hermitian reflections + clock generators, exact), ALGEBRAICALLY INDEPENDENT (exact Jacobian det nonzero at 3 exact points off the mirrors), degrees (8,12,20,24) Molien-unique with product 46080 = |G31| => by Chevalley [cited] a system of BASIC INVARIANTS: the holomorphic restriction of the W(E8) invariant ring generates the FULL G31 invariant ring; the Jacobian carries the 60 mirror lines (deg Jac = 60 = sum(d_i - 1), point-verified 60/60 on-mirror vanishing; full factorization = cited theorem, NAMED residual).  MUST-FAIL CONTROLS adjudicated: J' = RJR^T (not root-preserving) BREAKS the informative half {14,18,22,26,30} while the trivial isotropy layers persist; the root-preserving J'' keeps the full pattern (the theorem is about the W(E8)-conjugacy class of compiler-compatible J); a random non-isotropic 4-space breaks even F_2.  No marker move.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/quartic_half_probe.py (2026-08-03, 22/22, QUARTIC-HALF-ALIVE)."),
    ("v691_hecke_sos", "PRIME.HECKESOS.01: Hecke-equivariant sum of squares -- OFFENSIVE 4 (contract PRIME.W3.HECKE.SOS.01): search for the prime-local, Hecke-equivariant factorisation A = B*B + P (P >= 0) of the deployed Weil window form, with B from commuting prime channels and NO zero input; six verbatim acceptance criteria adjudicated (27 checks, ~12 s; discovery probe hecke_sos_probe.py 27/27, verdict HECKE-SOS-IHARA-MECHANISM-EXTRACTED).  [E, central] THE IHARA LAB (H2): the target factorisation EXISTS EXACTLY there -- A_IH = G_C + G_S with B = Chebyshev columns of the Hecke operator (recursion, NO Cholesky, NO spectrum) and P = G_S the closed defect Gram; P >= 0 <=> Ramanujan -- the RH analogue sits in ONE operator inequality Pi(I - Ahat^2) >= 0.  SHARPENING (the index lemma): the deployed zeta window form is, after index reversal, EXACTLY the sine/defect HALF of the canonical cos/sin split -- precisely the part whose positivity in the proven lab IS the RH analogue; the cos half is unconditionally SOS (PSD even on the violators).  [MEASURED] THE EULER MECHANISM (H1): commensurable fake primes break positivity EXACTLY on the resonance lattice 2 pi j/log 2 (median dev 0.0000, 12/12 snapped cells) and DEEPER than matched random jitter (depth ratio 1.98 >= 1.2) -- the incommensurability of the log p is a measured part of the cancellation (honest: the razor-thin W3 margin dies under ANY O(0.1) position damage, calibration (c) documented); NO exact B from channels (log p / D incommensurable, O3 census).  [MEASURED] H3 (symbol/Bochner): the deployed lag sequence is NOT a positive moment sequence (min sigma_B < 0 above t* too) -- positivity lives strictly in the odd sector (= the sine/defect half, coherent with H2); the multiplicative ansatz finds comb-spike POSITIONS but stays approximate (dead as exact SOS, alive as diagnostic).  CONTROLS all correct: Epstein fails as demanded (symbol dip + npp share localized), the Ihara trio passes with prisms breaking in the defect, scramble breaks.  THE ZETA GAP NAMED: Z1 missing -- a self-adjoint geometric operator whose polynomial traces are the window moments (Hilbert-Polya); Z2 (norm bound) would be RH itself -- the factorisation LOCALIZES RH, it does not bypass it (-> PRIME.Z1.OPERATOR.01, Offensive 5 running).  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/hecke_sos_probe.py (2026-08-03, 27/27, HECKE-SOS-IHARA-MECHANISM-EXTRACTED)."),
    ("v692_rank3_lockgram", "PRIME.RANK3LOCKGRAM.01: typing T-B through the zero side -- OFFENSIVE 2d: the deployed 2x2 lock block as an almost-collinear Gram matrix (7 checks, ~20 s; discovery probe rank3_lockgram_probe.py 7/7).  [E] THE DECOMPOSITION: via the v677 master identity, polarized, Ahat2 = G_Z + P + tail per entry (declared bar; T163 re-check t^T A t = B2 - S2): a POSITIVE zero-Gram G_Z (per-zero 2x2 psd of rank <= 2, Cauchy-Schwarz manifest per gamma) plus a psd RANK-1 pole layer P = c_P s s^T (closed form).  [E] THE MARGIN IDENTITY: det(G_Z + P) = det G_Z + c_P (s_perp^T G_Z s_perp) -- the razor-thin T-B margin IS the TRANSVERSE ZERO MASS, a sum of squares of the mass the zeros place orthogonal to the pole direction in the 2D lock space (gamma_1 alone carries 3..61% of it).  [E] SUPERADDITIVITY CERTIFICATE: on-line zeros can only INCREASE det (2x2 psd superadditivity; zeros 2e4 < gamma <= 3e12 on-line by citation Platt-Trudgian 2021): the truncation is safe-side.  THE TYPING: 'E kippt nicht' is a QUANTIFIED PARTIAL-RH TAIL statement -- NOT a 2c-envelope question and NOT a W3 renaming in 2D: the only threat is off-line quadruples above the cited 3e12.  CENSUS: T-B(block) closes on 8/15 verification windows at 3e12 alone, 13/15 under the named density route; the remainder carries exact factors (worst 1428) and finite required heights T* up to 1.1e16.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/rank3_lockgram_probe.py (2026-08-03, 7/7)."),
    ("v693_rank3_density_close", "PRIME.RANK3DENSITY.01: closing T-B(block) with cited explicit zero-density bounds -- OFFENSIVE 2e (5 checks, ~100 s; discovery probe rank3_density_close_probe.py 5/5).  CITATION LEDGER [A-cited, exact forms]: [A1] Platt-Trudgian 2021 (RH to 3e12), [A2] Hasanalizade-Shen-Wong 2022 (explicit RvM count), [A3] functional-equation halving, [A4] the explicit Ingham-form zero density arXiv:2507.15184 (2025, Cor. 1 + Table 1, valid from exactly T >= 3e12); Simonic 2020 honestly listed as trivial in our T-range (needs T > 3e38), KLN/Bellotti superseded by [A4].  [E] THE REFINED SAFE-SIDE ENVELOPE: sinh difference pairing (exact lag-difference convolution, NOT the crude ||f||_1^2 (e^{2 a delta}-1)), V(0) = 0 (near-line off-line zeros are harmless), on-line subtraction of the certified count below 3e12 (~x2), Abel + Stieltjes tail: PEN drops x6.5..x14.4 vs the 2d worst case.  THE CENSUS: 60/70 complete frame-A windows close UNCONDITIONALLY-MODULO-CITATIONS (verification set 13/15); open remainder exact: 9 windows with T*_expl in [1.0e13, 3.0e13] + h=5690 at 8.5e14.  [MEASURED] extension beyond the family grows ~ e^{3.74 a} (the declared surface is a FINITE family of 70 complete windows -- window-by-window closure is a valid uniformity route).  Honest scope: this closes the determinant of the 2x2 LOCK block; full window positivity (W3, all modes) remains the conjecture.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/rank3_density_close_probe.py (2026-08-03, 5/5)."),
    ("v694_interpolation_lemma_closure", "PRIME.INTERPCLOSURE.01: closing the two named building blocks of the alias-interpolation lemma (PRIME.W3.INTERPOLATION.01 follow-up; 20 checks, ~19 s; discovery probe interpolation_lemma_closure_probe.py 20/20, verdict CLOSURE-BOTH-NEAR-PROOF).  (iii) RETENTION [E]: exact projection identity Im Phi_x(z0) = ||(I - Pi)m||^2, closed-form O(k^2) certificate (geometric F-sums + Gram eigenvalue) valid on every read; measured uniform floor r_f >= 0.548 over the standard family surface, >= 0.266 on subcritical adversarial clusters; BOUNDARY CASE discovered: a straddling sub-resolution real pair collapses the pinned filter (derivative-pin mechanism) but the detector still fires there via the barred Ritz/k=0 branch and retention recovers with alpha; Ingham 1936 covers the Gram at q > 1 (measured k-stable plateau).  (v) SEPARATION LAW [MEASURED], FORM-CORRECTED: synthetic alpha-scaling (own Lambda sieve to 4.9e8, assembly == core, per-lag Weil verified) REJECTS the pure law alpha* = C'/dg and establishes the ADDITIVE law alpha* = C_cell/delta1 + C''/dg with C''_med = 0.494, C''_up = 0.590, adjudication-tight (constructed menu == eigen verdict up to one grid step), ZERO exceptions in 97 tests; the two family-blind parent configs detect at alpha* = 7.90 -- the family-alpha undetectability was exactly the resolution gap, now quantified; C''(n = 3) ~ 2x pair value = the declared residue.  Residues: explicit Ingham constant chain (classical bookkeeping), the Dirichlet-kernel overlap bound (elementary, unwritten), the C''(n) induction.  An off-line zero is the HYPOTHESIS of every statement; no RH claim, no marker move.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/interpolation_lemma_closure_probe.py (2026-08-03, 20/20, CLOSURE-BOTH-NEAR-PROOF)."),
    ("v695_z1_trace_operator", "PRIME.Z1MEASURE.01: the Z1 search, OFFENSIVE 5 (contract PRIME.Z1.OPERATOR.01) -- does a self-adjoint, GEOMETRICALLY constructed operator exist (zeta-free, zero-free, AST-enforced) whose polynomial traces generate the Weil window moments? (25 checks, ~3 s; discovery probe z1_trace_operator_probe.py 25/25, verdict Z1-MEASURE-FROM-COUNTING-OPERATOR-OPEN).  CANDIDATE CENSUS (round 1): (i) SEAM (v621/v622/v623) DEAD as Z1 spectrum -- traces on 48Z/16Z carriers closed but residuals ~1 despite the one global scalar, spectral phases = arithmetic progression, t-positions drift with 1/D against the window-invariant target spikes; lives as scaffold lab (NS sector = automatic trivial-mode subtraction).  (ii) E8 COUNTING (v625/G1): THE MEASURE LIVES, THE OPERATOR IS MISSING -- atoms EXACT from the shell recursion (to n = 20000, Satake normalizer = lattice data, dev 0.0e+00), arch + pole via the closed Gamma duplication split (the held line carries s = 0, 1), 7/8 target spikes reproduced (q = 0.000, window covariance passes); must-fail: without the Satake projection the form breaks -- the projection is load-bearing.  (iii) ORBIFOLD (v679) DEAD as Z1 -- conformal towers are APs and the comb carries NO AP structure beyond chance (null-calibrated, both quantiles >> 0.05).  [E] THE PRECISION FROM Z1a: the deployed window symbol sigma_B is SIGNED (Toeplitz sections indefinite 5/5), BUT the comb sequence c + pole is POSITIVE-FEASIBLE (both test windows; wrong sign breaks): the positive spectral object EXISTS and is the zero comb -- the signedness of the deployed sequence IS the pole subtraction (tau = positive comb trace - closed rank-2 pole functional).  Kill criteria K-A..K-D preregistered (zeta/zero loading = renaming, AST-enforced; AP spectra excluded; no per-window fit).  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/z1_trace_operator_probe.py (2026-08-03, 25/25, Z1-MEASURE-FROM-COUNTING-OPERATOR-OPEN)."),
    ("v696_z1_jacobi", "PRIME.Z1JACOBI.01: Z1 canonical construction, OFFENSIVE 5b -- Verblunsky / CMV / Jacobi from the positive comb sequence c + pole (18 checks, ~1 s; discovery probe z1_jacobi_probe.py 18/18, verdict Z1-JACOBI-OPAQUE with the strong renaming clause explicitly NOT confirmed).  [E] THE CANONICAL OPERATOR EXISTS: CMV unitary (367x367) + Jacobi self-adjoint (Wheeler/modified-Chebyshev on the Chebyshev moments), machine-verified back-direction: ALL moments reproduced, worst rel dev 2e-13 -- Z1 is now PURELY the closed-form question for the coefficient sequences.  [MEASURED] NO closed law: the two NAMED first-order laws fail (log-symbol r = +0.05, counting link r = +0.10; max|alpha| = 0.24 is nonperturbative -- this rules out the named laws, not every closed form), the h-ladder fails (min r_env = -0.13: the u-profile tracks alpha, not h -- no continuum kernel yet).  BUT the counting signature is PRESENT: feature positions on the prime-power slots at q = 0.000, amplitude-mass link r_log = +0.76, and positivity is LOAD-BEARING -- smooth/scramble controls lose PD entirely at k ~ 170/171 while the true masses stay PD to 2865: the coefficients are counting-structured but not yet closed-form-named.  IHARA ANCHOR: Kesten-McKay density exact, girth corrections measured.  Contract note update PRIME.Z1.OPERATOR.01.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/z1_jacobi_probe.py (2026-08-03, 18/18, Z1-JACOBI-OPAQUE)."),
    ("v697_z1_uvarov", "PRIME.Z1UVAROV.01: the slot-amplitude transfer law, OFFENSIVE 5c -- exact point-mass / single-lag insertion machinery for the Z1 coefficient response (14 checks, ~1 s; discovery probe z1_uvarov_probe.py 14/14, verdict Z1-UVAROV-SEQUENTIAL-CLOSED).  [E] DUALITY PROVEN: the atoms are LAG-SIDE insertions, NOT orthogonality-measure point masses (those sit at the zeros = the renaming direction, firewalled); the literal Uvarov/CD-kernel machinery is implemented and distinguishes the two.  [E] THE EXACT TRANSFER IDENTITY: Delta alpha_{m0-1} = w_1/E_{m0-1} (dev 5.6e-17; E = Toeplitz det ratio = ||Phi||^2, the position-free Christoffel object), zero response below the slot (locality exact).  [MEASURED] THE INVERTED STABILIZATION LAW: the Gamma flow (arch+pole background) PREDICTS the counting masses to ~10% -- median ratio 1.026 in [0.90, 1.15], IQR width 0.138, corr 0.86, family medians in [0.8, 1.3] (window-4 census) -- the flow knows the masses, not vice versa.  [E] COMPOSITION SEQUENTIAL-EXACT: Z1 = canonical CMV/Jacobi of arch+pole background + ONE single-lag insertion per prime power (<= 2 adjacent cells at m0 = u_n/D, weights = linear split of -mu_n/2, counting data only), with just-in-time positivity (prefix margins >= 0, 1-11 lags); every prime power individually load-bearing (removals break PD).  Contract note update PRIME.Z1.OPERATOR.01.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/z1_uvarov_probe.py (2026-08-03, 14/14, Z1-UVAROV-SEQUENTIAL-CLOSED)."),
    ("v698_z1_flow_recursion", "PRIME.Z1FLOWREC.01: positions, residual, E-transport, OFFENSIVE 5d -- is the whole prime comb forced by the arch+pole flow? (15 checks, ~20 s; discovery probe z1_flow_recursion_probe.py 15/15, verdict Z1-RECURSION-SEMI).  [MEASURED] POSITIONS FORCED: per-slot windows 0.5-2 cells (6/6 sharp), jitter null 30/30 (no jittered comb reaches the true objective), adversary deficit -516 lags -- the prime-power positions are pinned by the flow, not fitted.  [MEASURED] SHOOTING: too-light and too-heavy insertions diverge through OPPOSITE channels (reflection coefficient k -> +1 vs k -> -1), so bisecting on sign(k_bd) recovers the counting mass at the true position to median |0.11|% -- the Z1 recursion is a SHOOTING PROBLEM: the counting mass is the unique value threading the flow between the two divergence channels.  [E] slot identity dev 9.4e-14 (5c machinery re-verified).  HONEST NEGATIVES: autonomous reconstruction fails at greedy saturation (1/6 windows; lookahead missing), the residual after arch+pole+primes is noise-like (no further structure found), the E-transport is recursive (each insertion updates E) -- PRIME.Z1.OPERATOR.01 stays OPEN: the continuum reading is missing.  The zero-side read is a firewalled CORRELATION DIAGNOSTIC only (AST-confined to p2_zero_diagnostic, feeds nothing back).  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/z1_flow_recursion_probe.py (2026-08-03, 15/15, Z1-RECURSION-SEMI)."),
    ("v699_cone_dynamics", "QGEO.CONEDYN.01: cone dynamics -- the review-7.3 question ('use the Lorentz form DYNAMICALLY instead of statically') executed on the prime-front determinant coordinates y(a) = (S11, S22, S12)(a) with J_det of signature (1,2) (18 checks, <1 s; discovery probe cone_dynamics_probe.py 18/18, verdict CONE-DYNAMICS-DEAD).  THE HONEST KILL: (i) prime updates are TRANSLATIONS in y-space (linearity verified exactly: the per-prime increment is y-independent), so no multiplicative cone-preserving semigroup exists; (ii) ~99% of the increments are SPACELIKE (violating fractions 0.009-0.014 per family are the cone-preserving exceptions' complement witness), ell is NOT monotone on the true path (decreasing fractions 0.001-0.014); (iii) no Perron-Frobenius/Lorentz-boost reading of the prime flow survives the measurements.  SIDE FINDING (alive): the LEAF FUNCTIONAL separates scramble/Epstein controls where det is blind (C3.SEP: all 3 scramble seeds + Epstein separate on >= 1 window each).  AST zero-firewall (no zeta, no zeros); deterministic; Lambda_E machinery verbatim from the epstein firewall probe.  A DEAD verdict promoted for the record: the review-7.3 dynamic-cone route is closed, the static cone results (v624/v627) stand untouched.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/cone_dynamics_probe.py (2026-08-03, 18/18, CONE-DYNAMICS-DEAD)."),
    ("v700_orbit60_census", "E8.ORBIT60.01: the ORBIT60 census -- the 60 mu4-lines of E8 as a combinatorial object: quotient graph, sigma/clock/Coxeter dynamics on the ORBIT SPACE, and a STRICT park test for the cascade 60 -> 6 (18 checks, ~1 s; discovery probe orbit60_census_probe.py 18/18, verdict ORBIT60-PARKED).  THE FIVE ROUTES, all adjudicated: (i) degree rules DEAD (all quotient graphs regular -- no distinguished pair sequence from incidence degrees); (ii) sigma structure DEAD (sigma-orbit sizes {3,1} on the lines, no 2-blocks); (iii) INVOLUTION WITNESS DOES NOT EXIST: the full involution census of the line group LG (order 11520; 375 involutions, 21 conjugacy classes) shows NO element of cycle type 2^27 1^6 (fixed-line census {0: 120, 4: 180, 12: 15, 16: 60}) -- the one-shot group-action carrier of the cascade is absent; (iv) reflection/Coxeter DEAD: W(E8) Coxeter dynamics does not descend (reflection cycle types on the lines all equal, no distinguished element with 27 disjoint 2-blocks); (v) MUST-FAIL numerology control fires as designed: rule-free lexicographic pair removal reproduces the counting 60 - 2n in exactly 27 steps and > 10^70 equally 'successful' sequences exist -- the counting carries no structural information.  A5 one-liner (as instructed, no expedition): order-5 elements exist (2304) but <sigma, sample order-5> has order 960 -- no visible natural A5 action.  PARKED per the review protocol; the cascade stays a numerological observation, not a structure.  Deterministic (fixed seed for the generating-set search only).  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/orbit60_census_probe.py (2026-08-03, 18/18, ORBIT60-PARKED)."),
    ("v701_big_picture_hunt", "PRIME.KEYSTONE.01: the BIG-PICTURE HUNT -- cheap machine reads for the deep-analysis question 'does the missing rest of the RH program already sit in the corpus?' (11 checks, <1 s; discovery probe big_picture_hunt_probe.py 11/11).  THE KEYSTONE [E]: the deployed window form B is EXACTLY the sine-moment form of (c + pole) plus a rank-1 pole square -- one identity gluing the v695 measure route to the v677 master identity; with it the three named gaps of the program COLLAPSE ONTO ONE (defect positivity modulo the operator question: the signedness is the pole subtraction, resolved at the identity level).  THE TRIPLICATION IDENTITY [E]: the zeta arch density is the MEAN OF THREE DIGAMMA CHANNELS on the zeta_12 period grid (arguments 1/12, 5/12, 3/4), and mu_3 is the UNIQUE order for which the channel mean reproduces the arch (mu_2/mu_4/mu_6 all fail) -- the first exact bridge from the arch layer to the deck-sector geometry.  THE HONEST KILL: the V5 fixpoint numerology is DEAD (PSLQ finds no integer relation; the fixpoint carries no arithmetic).  No zeros read anywhere (zeta VALUES only in one declared diagnostic constant).  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/big_picture_hunt_probe.py (2026-08-03, 11/11)."),
    ("v702_z1_lookahead", "PRIME.Z1LOOKAHEAD.01: OFFENSIVE 5e -- the lookahead problem: autonomous zeta-free reconstruction of the prime comb from the Gamma flow (13 checks, ~30 s; discovery probe z1_lookahead_probe.py 13 PASS / 0 FAIL, verdict Z1-RECURSION-SEMI sharpened to FLOW-VERIFIER-NOT-GENERATOR).  [MEASURED] THE FLOW VERIFIES: the full true comb is flow-verified (913 >= 898 on the declared objective) and EVERY fake comb dies >= 184 lags earlier -- the Gamma flow is a comb VERIFIER of full depth.  [MEASURED] THE FLOW DOES NOT GENERATE: both prescribed lookahead routes (depth-2 beam search with adaptive horizon-3 deepening; global DP over the slot lattice) reach only 2-4 slots autonomously; the per-slot information demand g ~ 5-12 bits is INFORMATION-THEORETIC (measured from the surviving-candidate counts) and parameter-robust -- autonomous generation needs input the background flow does not carry at this resolution.  The 5d state stands: positions + masses forced CONDITIONED on the exact past; the continuum reading stays the remainder; PRIME.Z1.OPERATOR.01 stays OPEN.  AST-enforced zero firewall.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/z1_lookahead_probe.py (2026-08-03, 13/13, Z1-RECURSION-SEMI / FLOW-VERIFIER-NOT-GENERATOR)."),
    ("v703_chain_tolerance_scaling", "PRIME.CHAINTOL.01: S-A, THE CIRCULARITY DECIDER -- how sharply does the Z1 flow-induction constrain the counting masses? (10 checks, ~60 s; discovery probe chain_tolerance_scaling_probe.py 10/10, verdict TOLERANCE-RH-GRADE).  THE DECISION: the per-step mass tolerance an autonomous flow induction would need shrinks to RH-GRADE (and OVER-RH on the fine windows) -- the tolerance induction as a proof route is DEAD, and honestly so: any procedure meeting the tolerance would already know the masses to a precision equivalent to the open problem.  THE POSITIVE STRUCTURE: the Levinson recursion is an UNSTABLE SHOOTING problem -- generic mass perturbations diverge geometrically and the TRUE comb is the unique bounded trajectory (the v698 shooting picture at chain level); the budget comparison quantifies the gap between delivered and demanded tolerance per window.  AST zero-firewall (budgets are elementary closed forms).  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_tolerance_scaling_probe.py (2026-08-03, 10/10, TOLERANCE-RH-GRADE)."),
    ("v704_chain_mass_law", "PRIME.CHAINMASS.01: S-B, THE G1 EXACTNESS HUNT -- does a CLOSED formula (no per-slot fit, no per-window scalar) predict the counting masses from the flow? (5 checks, <1 s; discovery probe chain_mass_law_probe.py 5/5, verdict G1-OPEN).  THE CENSUS: seven closed candidate laws (Levinson orders, minimax ramps, Christoffel variants) are scored on three windows; the BEST closed law is C2 (zero reflection coefficient at the NEXT Levinson order m_hi+2): median ratio 0.9947, IQR [0.9853, 1.0086] -- but max|ratio-1| = 0.3130 on the soft slots, far above the 0.1% exactness bar: G1 stays OPEN as a closed-form question.  THE STRATA (declared): weak |a_bg| slots carry the misses (median|r-1| 0.049), mid and tight strata sit at 0.010/0.006 -- the residual is background-conditioned, not uniform noise.  AST zero-firewall.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_mass_law_probe.py (2026-08-03, 5/5, G1-OPEN)."),
    ("v705_chain_deck_sector", "QGEO.DECKSECTOR.01: S-C, THE V3 OPERATOR TARGET -- do the three digamma channels of the zeta arch density (arguments 1/12, 5/12, 3/4 on the zeta_12 grid) come from the seam geometry? (7 checks, <1 s; discovery probe chain_deck_sector_probe.py 7/7).  THE GEOMETRY ANCHOR: the three digamma channels ARE the three deck sectors of the 48-site NS lift -- computed as exact tower traces of the v623 deck sectors with the v628 twists {1/6, 1/2, 5/6}, they reproduce the arch density channel by channel at deviation 3.4e-16, the relative scalar is FORCED to 1 (not fitted), and the must-fail control (wrong twist set) is off by x82.  This closes the v701 triplication identity INTO the geometry: the arch layer of the Weil measure is a deck-sector trace of the seam orbifold -- the first operator-shaped reading of the arch.  Deterministic, exact arithmetic where declared.  No marker move (GATE.QGEO untouched), no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_deck_sector_probe.py (2026-08-03, 7/7)."),
    ("v706_chain_weyl_mass", "PRIME.WEYLMASS.01: S-D, THE WEYL CHARACTERIZATION OF G1 -- is the exact mass law an evaluation of the m-/Schur function of the background operator? (10 checks, ~10 s; discovery probe chain_weyl_mass_probe.py 10/10, verdict WEYL-NULL).  THE HONEST NULL: the point-evaluation reading (mass = Weyl function evaluated at the slot) is FALSIFIED (K2 median 0.3993, max 0.9293, corr 0.198 -- scramble-level).  THE POSITIVE FINDS: (i) the flow alpha ARE the Schur parameters of the background operator (identity verified at 1e-40) -- the chain arc's flow coordinates get an operator-theoretic name; (ii) the background breakdown sits EXACTLY between the n=2 and n=3 cell (the corridor boundary is an operator feature, not a tuning); (iii) the bare Gamma flow knows log 2 to 0.1-0.6% (bootstrap median|r-1| 0.0397) -- the binary-lattice constant is carried by the background alone.  AST zero-firewall.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_weyl_mass_probe.py (2026-08-03, 10/10, WEYL-NULL)."),
    ("v707_chain_section_edge", "PRIME.SECTIONEDGE.01: S-E, THE CLOSED FORM OF THE SECTION-POSITIVITY EDGE -- is the exact mass the Christoffel-Darboux / resolvent edge of the finite section? (9 checks, ~10 s; discovery probe chain_section_edge_probe.py 9/9, verdict EDGE-EXACT-SELECTION-OPEN).  [E] THE EDGE FORMULA IS EXACT: the section-positivity edge is a RESOLVENT IDENTITY (Christoffel-Darboux form), verified to 3e-13 -- the corridor edges of the just-in-time positivity picture (v697) now have a closed formula; the full-ladder edge pins the mass to 2.6e-04.  [MEASURED] THE SELECTION STAYS OPEN: the death-depth selection rule misses (max dev 0.964), the jit midpoint rule reaches max dev 0.064, and the TRUE mass sits at the jit corridor position median 0.534, IQR [0.511, 0.559] -- systematically NOT at an edge and NOT at the midpoint: 'explain the ~0.53' is the named open question of the chain arc.  AST zero-firewall.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_section_edge_probe.py (2026-08-03, 9/9, EDGE-EXACT-SELECTION-OPEN)."),
    ("v708_chain_position_functional", "PRIME.POSFUNC.01: S-F, THE POSITION FUNCTIONAL -- which functional fixes the corridor position ~0.53 that S-E left open? (7 checks, ~110 s; discovery probe chain_position_functional_probe.py 7/7, verdict FUNCTIONAL-OPEN).  THE CENSUS: of the preregistered functional families (edge distances, midpoints, energy extrema, curvature reads) the BEST is the LEVINSON ENERGY EXTREMUM E_{N-1}: median ratio 0.9986, max deviation 11.7% -- and it TRANSPORTS across windows without any per-window scalar (the strongest selection signal of the arc so far); none reaches the 1% uniform bar, so the selection principle stays OPEN.  THE OUTLIER STRUCTURE (declared): the misses sit EXACTLY on the prime powers 16/64/81 -- the same cells the Hecke mechanism (v710) later heals: the two findings interlock.  AST zero-firewall.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_position_functional_probe.py (2026-08-03, 7/7, FUNCTIONAL-OPEN)."),
    ("v709_chain_zero_layer", "PRIME.ZEROLAYER.01: S-G, THE LAYERING HYPOTHESIS (DIAGNOSTIC) -- is the S-F selection residual a zero-comb layer? (10 checks, ~70 s; discovery probe chain_zero_layer_probe.py 10/10, verdict LAYERING-REJECTED).  THE CLEAN NULL: in all tested projections the energy-extremum residual carries NO zero signature -- best correlation 0.042 (V1, s = 0.20), exactly the scramble level; the alternative read corr(res, von-Mangoldt defect) = -0.059 and removing it leaves max 0.1199 of 0.1172 (nothing explained).  THE DECOMPOSITION: ~64% of the residual is WINDOW GEOMETRY (grid/resolution artifacts), the rest unattributed noise.  THE DISCIPLINE: the zero data enter through a TEMPORAL SHA256 FIREWALL -- the residual is hashed and frozen BEFORE any zero is read, so no leakage from the zero side into the residual construction is possible.  An honest diagnostic null promoted for the record: the chain residual is not secretly the zeros.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_zero_layer_probe.py (2026-08-03, 10/10, LAYERING-REJECTED)."),
    ("v710_chain_two_stage_hecke", "PRIME.TWOSTAGE.01: P1 KILL TEST -- the two-stage Hecke selector for the G1 residual (7 checks, ~55 s; discovery probe chain_two_stage_hecke_probe.py 7/7, verdict P1-TWO-STAGE-DEAD).  THE MEMO KILL FIRED: the two-stage selector misses its own preregistered bar (max overall deviation 6.15% > 2%) -- the composite closed law is dead as stated.  THE MECHANISM THAT SURVIVES: the HECKE STAGE heals exactly the prime-power cells 11.7% -> 0.53% (the v708 outliers), and its channel detection is CIRCLE-FREE from the E8 counting [E] (Satake from shell counts, no zeta input) -- the prime-power corrections are geometric, not fitted.  THE REMAINDER NAMED: what is left is the FIRST-BIRTH selection error on coarse windows -- measured next in v711; G1 = [E-edge] + [E-Hecke] + [M-rate] is the resulting typed decomposition.  AST zero-firewall.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_two_stage_hecke_probe.py (2026-08-03, 7/7, P1-TWO-STAGE-DEAD)."),
    ("v711_chain_firstbirth_scaling", "PRIME.FIRSTBIRTH.01: P1b -- fit-free measurement of the first-birth selection error scaling with window resolution (7 checks, ~160 s; discovery probe chain_firstbirth_scaling_probe.py 7/7, verdict CONTINUUM-SELECTOR-MEASURED).  THE MEASUREMENT: the first-birth selection error CONVERGES under window refinement -- promotion-run power law theta = 1.851 (R^2 = 0.692) on the max statistic, ladder halves 2.736/1.520 both positive, late primes 1.866, resolved-horizon theta = 0.491; 0/30 primes non-converging; the finest 6 windows carry 0 degenerate-horizon slots (the big outliers are exactly the cells where the next atom is < 2 cells away -- pure geometry).  Preregistered bars theta >= 0.5, R^2 >= 0.6: the run-to-run spread of the point estimate (worker run theta ~ 1.25, R^2 ~ 0.90) stays far inside the bars -- a ONE-DECADE law, extrapolation honestly typed [M].  With v707/v710 this completes the typed G1 decomposition [E-edge] + [E-Hecke] + [M-rate]: the continuum selector is MEASURED, not proven.  AST zero-firewall.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/chain_firstbirth_scaling_probe.py (2026-08-03, 7/7, CONTINUUM-SELECTOR-MEASURED)."),
    ("v712_rank3_transverse_deck", "PRIME.RANK3TRANSV.01: P4 MAIN STRIKE -- transverse scalarization x deck triplication for the ten open T-B windows at citation height 3e12 (5 checks, ~65 s; discovery probe rank3_transverse_deck_probe.py 5/5).  THE P4 THEOREM-LEVEL MOVE: the v692 margin identity is SCALARIZED along the transverse direction (the penalty pays only the transverse mass, not the full matrix norm) -- median improvement x4.23 on the open-10 -- and the census closes 9 of the 10: **69/70 complete family windows now close at the cited 3e12** (unconditional-modulo-citations, the v693 ledger); the remainder is EXACTLY ONE window, h = 5690, with certificate height T* = 1.6e14 (down from 8.5e14).  THE HONEST NEGATIVE: the deck-triplication lever is DEAD by the triangle inequality (channel sups can only lose; verified exact on the deck split) -- the deck geometry helps the arch reading (v705), not the T-B margin.  Zeros <= 2e4 enter the MARGIN only (RvM-checked); the penalty uses no zero data.  Parents v684/v692/v693 imported read-only; caches repo-relative.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/rank3_transverse_deck_probe.py (2026-08-03, 5/5, 69/70)."),
    ("v713_l1_montage", "PRIME.L1MONTAGE.01: L1-MONTAGE -- the first explicit assembly of the CONTINUUM candidate of the Z1 operator and the machine test of its declared limit gates (16 checks, ~1 s; discovery probe l1_montage_probe.py 16/16, verdict L1-ASSEMBLED-MEASURED).  THE ASSEMBLY: the continuum candidate is MOUNTED from the corpus pieces (S-C deck-sector arch + 5c lag-insertion atoms + v695 pole subtraction): the cover limit converges at 6.2e-8, the point masses converge at the D^2 rate, and exactly ONE UV slot remains (the declared ultraviolet boundary of the construction).  THE REPAIR: the 5b negative (no h-stable alpha ladder) was a NORMALIZATION ARTIFACT -- rescaled, the ladder stabilizes (M2.2-M2.4).  THE BOUNDARY: the montage diverges EXACTLY at s <= 1/2 -- the critical line appears as the natural boundary of the construction, honestly typed as a consistency signature, NOT a positivity statement.  THE MISSING THEOREMS ARE NAMED (self-adjointness of the limit, trace identification, positivity) -- named, not claimed; PRIME.Z1.OPERATOR.01 stays OPEN.  AST zero-firewall (banned names checked).  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/l1_montage_probe.py (2026-08-03, 16/16, L1-ASSEMBLED-MEASURED)."),
    ("v714_moonshot_hecke_groupoid", "PRIME.MOONSHOT.01: MOONSHOT first slice -- the E8 Hecke groupoid tower: is the ATOM LAYER of the Weil measure groupoid-internal? (19 checks, ~10 s; discovery probe moonshot_hecke_groupoid_probe.py 19/19, verdict MOONSHOT-GO).  THE GO: the atom layer IS groupoid-internal from the Z[i]-E8 Hecke tower -- (i) the primitive degrees of the tower are EXACTLY the Gaussian prime norms (maximality census; no prime projector is used anywhere -- the primes come OUT of the tower, they are not put in); (ii) the log generator + cell normalizer DE-DIVISORIZE the tower traces at 4e-13 (von Mangoldt from divisor sums, closed); (iii) the sigma descent reproduces 100 atom positions, 100 masses and 368 moments at deviation 0.00 against the L1 point masses.  DECLARED INGREDIENTS: the sqrt(n) half-density and the sigma descent -- both named as inputs, not derived.  THE HONEST FENCE (typed): the finite counting facts used in this slice are E8-UNSPECIFIC -- the SPECIFICITY question (does the tower single out E8 among lattices?) is STAGE 2, which also owns the arch layer (here still glued as a direct sum).  Contract PRIME.Z1.MOONSHOT.01 registered with the stage-2 gluing as the next gate.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/moonshot_hecke_groupoid_probe.py (2026-08-03, 19/19, MOONSHOT-GO)."),
    ("v715_qgeo_car_continuum", "QGEO.CARLIMIT.01: QGEO-CAR -- the quasi-free CAR route to the formal orbifold continuum limit (GATE.QGEO), first slice (22 checks, ~10 s; discovery probe qgeo_car_continuum_probe.py 22/22, verdict QGEO-CAR-RATES-SUMMABLE).  THE STRATEGY EXECUTED: not measure compactness -- the orbifold correlators are DETERMINANTS of a one-particle covariance, so the limit runs through SCHATTEN-NORM control plus Araki's quasi-free CAR theory.  THE MEASUREMENTS: all 6+1 deck/twist sector covariances AND all dressed twist channels are Schatten/shadow-norm CAUCHY on eps-separated configurations (N up to 3072 / 6144), with geometrically summable rates; the FH renormalization is FIT-FREE LATTICE-DERIVED (Barnes G, deviation 8.8e-7); the RP cone margins do NOT degenerate along the ladder; all four kill criteria are clear.  THE REMAINDER NAMED: the majorant lemma (L1)-(L3) is stated with constants and the CLASSICAL proof route (Hadamard three-lines / kernel domination) -- named, not claimed: GATE.QGEO does NOT move.  Deterministic (no RNG); self-contained.  No marker move.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/qgeo_car_continuum_probe.py (2026-08-03, 22/22, QGEO-CAR-RATES-SUMMABLE)."),
    ("v716_moonshot_arch_glue", "PRIME.MOONSHOT.02: MOONSHOT stage 2 -- the shared arch-sector test: does the archimedean place of the SAME Z[i]-E8 commensurability groupoid (stage 1, v714) deliver the arch tower of the Weil measure? (18 checks, ~3 s; discovery probe moonshot_arch_glue_probe.py 18/18, verdict MOONSHOT-STAGE2-GLUED).  THE GLUING: one object, ONE normalization -- pole 2cosh(t/2) MINUS arch rho(t) MINUS atom orbits, atoms from the stage-1 groupoid comb, arch from the 48-site NS lift heat trace, pole from the two boundary exponents; the free 3-scalar LSQ (kappa_at, kappa_ar, kappa_p) returns (1, 1, 1) to < 1e-12 on all 5 windows -- the strategy-council kill (c) ('arch glues only as a direct sum') falls at measurement level.  THE DERIVATIONS: the 1/4 in Re psi(1/4 + i tau/2) IS the mu4 fixed-sector offset (modes m == 1 mod 4, DERIVED, exact trace identity to 1.4e-10); log pi enters ONLY through the declared self-dual (Tate) UV cell (pinned at 2.2e-16) -- the exact arch mirror of the declared sqrt(n) half-density; lift ladder s* -> 1 at rate ~N^-2 (|s*_inf - 1| = 2.4e-7).  MUST-FAILS: mu2 tower residual 0.326, wrong mu4 class 1.000, wrong deck twists 0.474 -- E8 becomes forced AT THE GLUING (mu4 units + triality deck = a rank-4 hermitian unimodular Z[i] carrier = the Gaussian E8 by the cited v634/v689 identification), not at the finite places.  Missing theorems NAMED (groupoid trace formula, product formula, sigma-descent theorem, L1 continuum, positivity = the RH-level step).  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/moonshot_arch_glue_probe.py (2026-08-03, 18/18, MOONSHOT-STAGE2-GLUED)."),
    ("v717_moonshot_state", "PRIME.MOONSHOT.03: MOONSHOT stage 3 -- the positivity STRUCTURE of the glued object: is the Weil functional a STATE on the groupoid algebra? (21 checks, ~3 s; discovery probe moonshot_state_probe.py 21/21, verdict MOONSHOT-STAGE3-STATE-ON-TRUNCATIONS).  THE STATE: on every truncation the Weil functional IS a state, CONSTRUCTIVELY -- Levinson on the unified moment vector is PD (min headroom 0.76), exhibiting T as the GNS/CMV vector state <e0, . e0> of the truncated translation flow; the convolution-positivity binding identity T(f*f~) = 2 V^T odd_toeplitz(c) V holds at 1e-12 over 80 battery vectors x 5 windows.  THE LOCALIZED RH SUBSTANCE: the naive regular-representation tower reading phi_pole + phi_orb does NOT give T -- the difference Delta (arch flow + atom interference) carries |Delta|/W3-margin = 104..1563: the trace-formula boundary is exactly where the conspiracy sits, now measured and typed.  KMS: the degree grading satisfies detailed balance M(-u) = e^{-u} M(u) at 1.1e-16 -- KMS-beta = 1, the Bost-Connes critical temperature; half-density exponent -1/2 MEASURED (-1/4 and -1 misfit hard); s = 1/2 = the symmetric GNS splitting.  CONTROLS calibrate both outcomes: Ihara/Petersen trace formula exact (states at every depth, finite unitary rep), Epstein x^2+5y^2 is NOT a state (67 negative Lambda sites, Levinson breakdown depth 49/62).  Missing theorems NAMED in order (trace formula, scaling limit, uniform symbol positivity = RH level, BC crossed-product KMS, E8 arch uniqueness).  No marker move, no RH claim -- outcome (i) only moves the quantifier into the limit.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/moonshot_state_probe.py (2026-08-03, 21/21, MOONSHOT-STAGE3-STATE-ON-TRUNCATIONS)."),
    ("v718_moonshot_spectral", "PRIME.MOONSHOT.04: MOONSHOT stage 4 -- the spectral identification: do the eigenvalues of the truncations of the glued object converge to the zeta zeros? (10 checks, ~33 s; discovery probe moonshot_spectral_probe.py 10/10, verdict MOONSHOT-STAGE4-SPECTRUM-CONVERGES-MEASURED).  DIAGNOSTIC TYPING (hard): the operator stays zeta-free (stage-2/3 unified measure); node predictions of every window are SHA256-FROZEN BEFORE the 379 target zeros are loaded in the one declared function.  THE MEASUREMENT: the largest window h = 1433 hits 100.0% of 377 zeros at tol 0.25 (97.1% at 0.10, 84.1% at 0.05, mean |dtau| = 0.0236); the h-ladder rate is -1.610 (power law) and the pure GNS K-ladder at fixed measure is MONOTONE 0.4678 -> 0.0153 -> 0.0042 -> 0.0003: the truncation eigenvalues move ONTO the zeros; unpartnered nodes are exactly the expected GNS picture (pole band, Gauss quadrature filling at density 3.37, UV edge).  CONTROLS: Ihara/Petersen rank-saturates and hits the graph spectrum at 2.2e-16 with exact weights (spectral identification EXACT where the trace formula is a theorem); SCRAMBLE (positions redrawn, masses kept): Levinson BREAKDOWN at depth 61 -- the scrambled measure is not even a state; GUE light (observation only): matched-node <r> = 0.6178 vs true zeros 0.6189 (GUE 0.5996, Poisson 0.3863).  HONESTY: a MEASUREMENT of the spectral identification, not a theorem -- it upgrades the trace-formula target to a precise interpolation statement.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/moonshot_spectral_probe.py (2026-08-03, 10/10, MOONSHOT-STAGE4-SPECTRUM-CONVERGES-MEASURED)."),
    ("v719_moonshot_traceformula", "PRIME.MOONSHOT.05: MOONSHOT Satz-1 slice -- the trace formula of the glued object, term by term against the classical Weil formula (24 checks, ~130 s; discovery probe moonshot_traceformula_probe.py 24/24, verdict MOONSHOT-SATZ1-LEDGER-EXACT).  F1 THE FINITE TRACE FORMULA IS EXACT: on every GNS truncation the Gauss-quadrature identity tr f(J_K) = sum w_i f(tau_i) = sum a_d p_d holds for every band-limited test (9 windows x 14 battery vectors, max rel dev 1.7e-11; ledger example dev 3.2e-14) -- and the TERM DICTIONARY to Weil 1952 CLOSES: pole block == int a~ 2cosh(u/2) (1.7e-13, the g(i/2)+g(-i/2) term), atom block == the classical prime term (1.8e-15), arch block == -int rho a~ (3.4e-16), UV cell == the stage-2 regularization (2.2e-16).  F2 DELTA IS CLASSICAL: the stage-3 difference term converges to [Gamma'/Gamma term] + [prime term] -- W_freq == W_len closed (5.6e-17), omega = 2 theta'_RS exact, deployed arch block = the Gamma'/Gamma term with sigma = 1.000161, c = -1.0e-4 (the one-sided sum honestly has NO limit: drift exactly log(2)/2 per D-halving); orbit interference is NOT aliasing -- it converges to the FULL classical prime term (rates measured); diagonal and pole square subleading.  F3 E8 UNIQUENESS AS A FINITE CENSUS: dimension-8 unimodular Z-lattices are classically {Z^8, E8} (Mordell 1938, declared); both carry Z[i] structure; parity fixes the mode tower -- ONLY the Gaussian E8 glues (kappa = 1, residual 8.5e-17; Z^8/mu2 rips at 0.102, wrong mu4 class at 0.314).  THE SATZ CANDIDATE is stated: everything geometric is classical Weil 1952 -- the new content sits EXCLUSIVELY in the convergence statements K1-K3.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/moonshot_traceformula_probe.py (2026-08-03, 24/24, MOONSHOT-SATZ1-LEDGER-EXACT)."),
    ("v720_moonshot_k2k3", "PRIME.MOONSHOT.06: MOONSHOT K2+K3 slice -- the two convergence theorems of the ledger list, measured and collapsed onto classical analysis (14 checks, ~3 s; discovery probe moonshot_k2k3_probe.py 14/14, verdict MOONSHOT-K2K3-COLLAPSED-CLASSICAL).  K3 -> TIGHTNESS: positivity is limit-stable, so K3 collapses onto K2 + tightness + identification -- measured: sum-gauge sum w_i == p_0 (2.9e-16), compacta masses Cauchy over the h-ladder, band-edge mass is UNDER the smooth omega density (resolution limit, no anomalous drain), Gauss tau-windows identify against the closed zeta-free classics (tau0 = 0/20 at 1.1e-5/3.9e-4; 60/120 follow the (D tau0)^2 Jackson law); the normalization subtlety is exact: p_0 = 0.981 log(1/D) - 1.306 -- T(1) grows like the smooth band density, the limit is SIGMA-FINITE (vague topology forced, no Prokhorov).  K2 -> CLASSICAL ON s > 1/2: clean error separation -- tail rates follow the smooth model on the whole s-battery (max slope deviation 0.000), the unconditional Chebyshev/PNT majorant 2 c_RS (s+1/2)/(s-1/2) X^{1/2-s} holds everywhere (c_RS = 1.03883 machine-verified in the sieve range), discretization ~ C D^2 (rates +1.55/+1.94); the slowdown law slope_X(s) == -(s - 1/2) is exact.  THE BOUNDARY: exactly s = 1/2 -- t = 0 diverges with Mertens slope 1.9994 == 2 in log X, t != 0 stays bounded; no earlier break.  THE LEDGER AFTER THIS SLICE: the hard substance concentrates in (L1) identification AT the line (no mass loss -- the RH substance) and (L2) K1 node convergence; (L3) is routine.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/moonshot_k2k3_probe.py (2026-08-03, 14/14, MOONSHOT-K2K3-COLLAPSED-CLASSICAL)."),
    ("v721_k1_node_capture", "PRIME.K1CAPTURE.01: K1 slice -- the node-capture lemma behind the stage-4 spectral measurement, built from classical quadrature theory and honestly adjudicated (14 checks, ~33 s; discovery probe k1_node_capture_probe.py 14/14, verdict K1-LEMMA-CAPTURE-ONLY).  THE LEMMA CHAIN (all implemented + verified): Markov-Stieltjes sandwich (0 violations over all nodes, synthetic lab + 9 real windows), the SYMMETRIZED Christoffel/Fejer bound w_j <= lambda_bd(x_j) everywhere (run-1 honesty: the unsymmetrized kernel bounds the wrong Christoffel function, max w/lambda = 1.9993 -- fixed to the theorem), and the DERIVED closed capture condition Lm(t+d) - RM(t-d) > 0 with certified radius d_pred; every synthetic peak (incl. a merged close pair) captures.  E4-pattern diagnostic typing: peaks/nodes/radii SHA256-frozen zeta-free BEFORE the target load.  THE ADJUDICATION (preregistered fork): capture validity >= 0.95 PASSES on the real windows, but the certified radii d_pred ~ 1.4-2.4 tau sit ~900x ABOVE the measured node errors (0.0003-0.03) -- the classical lemma carries the CAPTURE, NOT the super-resolution; the side finding: the bg-subtracted peak CENTROID beats the node -- the precision is TRACE-FORMULA content (the K1b question, exploration).  OFF-LINE HONESTY: the lemma presupposes mu >= 0 -- an off-line zero does not mislocate nodes, it breaks positivity (Levinson breakdown, the v688 falsifier route): capture lemma and falsifier are two sides of the SAME positivity premise; on the declared regime (frame-A, h <= 1433) PD is machine-verified per window.  No marker move, no RH claim.  Python-only per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/k1_node_capture_probe.py (2026-08-03, 14/14, K1-LEMMA-CAPTURE-ONLY)."),
